{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\n#define pb push_back\nusing namespace std;\nusing INT = long long;\nconst int mod = 1e9+7;\nint power(int a, int n, int mod, int ans=1) {\n    for(; n; n>>=1, a=(INT)a*a%mod) if(n & 1) ans = (INT)ans * a % mod;\n    return ans;\n}\n\nconst int NN = 1<<7;\nint p[NN][NN];\nint pro[NN][NN];\nint bpt[NN];\nINT q[NN][NN];\nint n;\nint id[NN];\nvector<int> vec[NN];\nmap<pair<int, INT>, int> mp;\n\ninline void add(int &u, int v) {u+=v; if(u>=mod) u -= mod;}\n\nint calc(int now, INT st) {\n    if(st == 0) return 0;\n    if(now == n) return 1;\n    if(mp.find({now, st}) != mp.end()) return mp[{now, st}];\n    int ans = 0;\n    for(int j=1; j<1<<n; j++) {\n        INT nst = 0;\n        for(int k=0; k<vec[now].size(); k++) {\n            if(not (st & (1LL<<k))) continue;\n            int cur = vec[now][k];\n            int nxt = j - (j&cur);\n            nst |= q[cur][nxt];\n        }\n        add(ans, (INT)pro[now][j] * calc(now+1, nst) % mod);\n    }\n    return mp[{now, st}] = ans;\n}\n\nint main(){\n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n    freopen(\"in.in\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"out.out\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif // ONLINE_JUDGE\n\n\tscanf(\"%d\",&n);\n    int r100 = power(100, mod-2, mod);\n    for(int i=0; i<n; i++) {\n        for(int j=0; j<n; j++) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", p[i]+j);\n            p[i][j] = (INT)p[i][j] * r100 % mod;\n        }\n    }\n    for(int i=0; i<n; i++) {\n        for(int j=0; j<1<<n; j++) {\n            pro[i][j] = 1;\n            for(int k=0; k<n; k++) if((j>>k)&1) {\n                pro[i][j] = (INT)pro[i][j] * p[i][k] % mod;\n            } else pro[i][j] = (INT)pro[i][j] * (mod+1-p[i][k]) % mod;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for(int i=0; i<1<<n; i++) bpt[i] = __builtin_popcount(i);\n    for(int i=0; i<1<<n; i++) vec[bpt[i]].pb(i), id[i] = vec[bpt[i]].size() - 1;\n\tfor(int i=0; i<1<<n; i++) {\n        for(int j=0; j<n; j++) if(not ((i>>j)&1)) q[i][1<<j] = 1LL<<id[i|(1<<j)];\n        for(int j=0; j<1<<n; j++) q[i][j] = q[i][j&-j] | q[i][j ^ (j&-j)];\n\t}\n\tcout << calc(0, 1) << endl;\n}\n\n                      \n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    mod = 10**9 + 7\n    r100 = pow(100, mod - 2, mod)\n\n    p = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            p[i][j] = int(next(it)) * r100 % mod\n\n    NN = 1 << n\n\n    # pro[now][mask] = probability that player 'now' beats exactly the set 'mask'\n    pro = [[1] * NN for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(NN):\n            val = 1\n            for k in range(n):\n                if (j >> k) & 1:\n                    val = val * p[i][k] % mod\n                else:\n                    val = val * (mod + 1 - p[i][k]) % mod\n            pro[i][j] = val\n\n    # popcount, vector of masks per popcount, id[mask] = index within its popcount group\n    bpt = [0] * NN\n    vec = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]          # vec[pop] holds masks of that popcount\n    id = [0] * NN\n    for i in range(NN):\n        pop = i.bit_count()\n        bpt[i] = pop\n        id[i] = len(vec[pop])\n        vec[pop].append(i)\n\n    # q[i][j] \u2013 bitmask of the ids of masks (i|(1<<bit)) for bits set in j\n    q = [[0] * NN for _ in range(NN)]\n    for i in range(NN):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if not ((i >> j) & 1):\n                q[i][1 << j] = 1 << id[i | (1 << j)]\n        for j in range(NN):\n            low = j & -j\n            q[i][j] = q[i][low] | q[i][j ^ low]\n\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def calc(now, st):\n        if st == 0:\n            return 0\n        if now == n:\n            return 1\n        ans = 0\n        for j in range(1, NN):\n            nst = 0\n            for k in range(len(vec[now])):\n                if (st >> k) & 1:\n                    cur = vec[now][k]\n                    nxt = j - (j & cur)          # bits of j that are not in cur\n                    nst |= q[cur][nxt]\n            ans = (ans + pro[now][j] * calc(now + 1, nst)) % mod\n        return ans\n\n    print(calc(0, 1))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.99\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.576278118089249e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -0.000567275274079293, -0.0041396645829081535, 0.0, -0.2520811855792999, -0.012555248104035854, -6.9141146923357155e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, -4.5060096454108134e-05, -0.022681456059217453, -0.005693173035979271, -1.5019384622573853, -1.2755313036905136e-05, -0.0016470688860863447, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.3232143828645349e-05, 0.0, -0.07889547944068909, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0011729273246601224, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, -5.602820692729438e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07,